      "math_academy_id": "q-117664",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-3}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3-x, & x<1 \\\\ 2x, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}(3-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{-3}^{1}+{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[3(1)-\\frac{(1)^{2}}{2}-3(-3)+\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{2}]+[(2)^{2}-(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =[12+4]+[4-1] \\\\  & =16+3 \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
